{ns}
{define: Bm base-fret 1 frets x 0 4 4 3 2} 
{define: Cadd9 base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 3 0} 
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: D4 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 3}
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: FOREVER YOUNG – Bob Dylan/Joan Baez}
{st: (Dylan)}
{artist: Bob Dylan; Joan Baez}
{composer: Bob Dylan}


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-4UoJ47SzjA  (Capo 2)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and (CaddG) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  This version is Joan's (gussied up as usual) cover of Dylan's classic.  Bob usually plays the chorus immediately after the first verse while Joan plays the first two verses together.

TIP:  (CaddG) is just (C) with pinky added to 1st string/3rd fret (g), and (Cadd9) is (C) with pinky added to 2nd string/3rd fret (d).

TIP:  If you're not fond of the (Bm) you can play a (D) instead.  And the (Gadd) and (CaddG) can be omitted as well.


